operating mode.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`MODE` (pin A1) \u2192 `GND` \u2014 per the datasheet, Logic 0 on MODE allows the IC to auto-switch into PFM (power-save) mode under light load, i.e. the board is configured for Auto PFM/PWM operation.\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"IC2 FAN53610AUC33X: MODE A1 wired to a vertical line at x\u2248783 running down to the y\u2248608 rail shared with VIN\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"MODE held high forces fixed-frequency PWM operation instead of auto PFM, which increases light-load quiescent loss and deviates from the intended design.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The EthernetAndPower sheet appears to tie the FAN53610 GND pin and MODE pin onto the input (BAT+/VIN) rail, contrary to the spec, which requires MODE to GND and GND to ground. The GND-to-input merge would be a serious short, but the trace reading is uncertain at this resolution.\"\n}",
